Chapter: CompositeEvents
  cites Uoaix chapter GamePackets

 A bounded ring of recent speech and combat packets that every other connection's pulse delivers once,
 in range, or to one listener alone. Packet bytes are copied into buffers allocated with the ring, because
 a callback's own allocations lie above the serving loop's scratch mark. Volatile: a restart empties it.
 256 rows hold a pulse's swings, health and deaths for eight links between one connection's pulses.
  CeEvent = record { sequence : Integer, serial : Integer, also : Integer, only : Integer, x : Integer, y : Integer,
    buffer : Integer, length : Integer, ghost : Boolean }
  CeRing = record { events : List CeEvent, next : Integer }
  ce-limit : Integer = 256
  ce-range : Integer = 18
  ce-bytes : Integer = 512
  ce-rows : Integer, List CeEvent -> List CeEvent
  ce-rows (i) (xs) = if i == ce-limit then xs
    else ce-rows (i + 1) (list-push xs (CeEvent { sequence = 0, serial = 0, also = 0, only = 0, x = 0, y = 0,
      buffer = alloc-bytes ce-bytes, length = 0, ghost = False }))
  ce-new : Integer -> CeRing
  ce-new (unused) = CeRing { events = ce-rows 0 (__list-with-capacity ce-limit), next = 1 }
  ce-copy : Integer, List Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ce-copy (buffer) (packet) (i) = if i == list-length packet then 0
    else let put = poke-byte buffer i (list-at packet i) in ce-copy buffer packet (i + 1)
  ce-add : CeRing, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> Integer
  ce-add (ring) (serial) (x) (y) (packet) = ce-add-to ring serial 0 0 x y packet
  ce-add-to : CeRing, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> Integer
  ce-add-to (ring) (serial) (also) (only) (x) (y) (packet) = if list-length packet > ce-bytes then 0
    else let row = list-at ring.events (int-mod ring.next ce-limit)
    in let copied = ce-copy row.buffer packet 0
    in let a = __record-set row "sequence" ring.next
    in let b = __record-set row "serial" serial
    in let g = __record-set row "also" also
    in let h = __record-set row "only" only
    in let k = __record-set row "ghost" False
    in let c = __record-set row "x" x
    in let d = __record-set row "y" y
    in let e = __record-set row "length" (list-length packet)
    in let f = __record-set ring "next" (ring.next + 1) in 1
  ce-near : CeEvent, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  ce-near (event) (x) (y) = event.x >= x - ce-range & event.x <= x + ce-range & event.y >= y - ce-range & event.y <= y + ce-range
 A ghost's words enter the ring clear and marked; a listener who is not dead and holds no Spirit Speak (UOX3 spiritspeak.js
 SOCK_SPIRITSPEAK) hears them in ghost speech.
  ce-add-ghost : CeRing, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> Integer
  ce-add-ghost (ring) (serial) (x) (y) (packet) = let added = ce-add-to ring serial 0 0 x y packet
    in if added == 0 then 0 else let marked = __record-set (list-at ring.events (int-mod (ring.next - 1) ce-limit)) "ghost" True in 1
  ce-pending : CeRing, Integer, Boolean, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List (List Integer) -> List (List Integer)
  ce-pending (ring) (listener) (clear) (x) (y) (heard) (i) (acc) = if i == ce-limit then acc
    else let event = list-at ring.events (int-mod (ring.next + i) ce-limit)
    in let wanted = event.sequence > heard & (if event.only /= 0 then event.only == listener
      else event.serial /= listener & event.also /= listener & ce-near event x y)
    in let bytes = if wanted then __buf-read-bytes event.buffer 0 event.length else []
    in let heard-as = if not wanted | clear | not event.ghost then bytes else list-at (ce-ghostly [bytes] 0 []) 0
    in ce-pending ring listener clear x y heard (i + 1) (if wanted then list-push acc heard-as else acc)
  ce-speech : List (List Integer), Integer, Integer, List (List Integer) -> List (List Integer)
  ce-speech (packets) (speaker) (i) (acc) = if i == list-length packets then acc
    else let p = list-at packets i
    in let spoken = list-length p > 7 & (list-at p 0 == #1C | list-at p 0 == #AE) & gp-u32 p 3 == speaker
    in ce-speech packets speaker (i + 1) (if spoken then list-push acc p else acc)
 Others hear a ghost in UO's ghost speech: every letter of the text (from byte 44 of 0x1C, 48 of 0xAE) becomes o or O.
 The copies are new lists, so the speaker's own reply keeps its words.
  ce-ghostly : List (List Integer), Integer, List (List Integer) -> List (List Integer)
  ce-ghostly (packets) (i) (out) = if i == list-length packets then out
    else let p = list-at packets i
    in ce-ghostly packets (i + 1) (list-push out (ce-ghost-text p (if list-at p 0 == #1C then 44 else 48) 0 (__list-with-capacity (list-length p))))
  ce-ghost-text : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  ce-ghost-text (p) (start) (i) (out) = if i == list-length p then out
    else let b = list-at p i
    in let letter = i >= start & ((b >= 65 & b <= 90) | (b >= 97 & b <= 122))
    in ce-ghost-text p start (i + 1) (list-push out (if not letter then b else if int-mod (i * 7 + b) 3 == 0 then 79 else 111))
